Package: BE
Version: 0.3.0
Date: 2026-07-29
Title: Bioequivalence Study Data Analysis
Description: Analyze bioequivalence study data with industrial strength. The statistical core is delegated to the 'sasLM' package, which reproduces 'SAS' PROC GLM output; this covers the analysis of variance, the least square means, and the confidence interval of a 2x2 crossover study. Sample size could be determined for various crossover designs, such as 2x2 design, 2x4 design, 4x4 design, Balaam design, Two-sequence dual design, and William design.
             Reference: Chow SC, Liu JP. Design and Analysis of Bioavailability and Bioequivalence Studies. 3rd ed. (2009, ISBN:978-1-58488-668-6).
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: sasLM (>= 1.0.1), rtf
